=== SUMMARY ===
✓ All three NotificationSettings regions implemented as HIG cards/sections in the same
  data + grouping + order; the web copyLink chrome reproduced; no charts/maps (none in
  source); SwiftUI-native (materials via TSGlassPanel, not hand-rolled glass — ADR-005).
✓ @MainActor @Observable BrowserNotificationsPageModel drives the view; no networking /
  no platform calls in the view body (ADR-004). The web local-state hooks (useWebPush,
  useNotificationListener, useSettings tab signals, useNotificationSoundPrefs) map onto
  injected seams (NotificationPermissionProviding / NotificationSoundPreviewing /
  BrowserNotificationsPreferencesStoring) — production wires UNUserNotificationCenter +
  a system cue + UserDefaults; previews/tests inject deterministic doubles.
✓ Adaptive macOS + iOS (ADR-002/006): the header reflows (size-class) and the page
  scrolls; #if os(iOS) only for size class / nav-bar inline / AudioServices cue.
✓ i18n: every visible literal via LocalizedStringKey / NSLocalizedString; web key names
  kept; zero hardcoded literals. a11y (ADR-015): combined header elements, per-control
  labels, the Test aria label, ≥44pt controls, light/dark + high-contrast via P2 tokens.
✓ Tokens (P2) for ALL color/spacing/typography/radius; no inline literals. No SI units
  on this surface (no measurements) — nothing stored/computed off-SI.
✓ Navigation: typed deep-link BrowserNotificationsLink + .browserNotificationsDestination()
  + BrowserNotificationsRouteRegistration.make() (sibling precedent — no shared-enum edit,
  Sources/App is out of allowed scope; web /notifications/browser has no AppRoute case).

